1
00:00:00,412 --> 00:00:02,052
(Wil:)Well, not everybody felt that way.

2
00:00:02,214 --> 00:00:03,754
(Wil:)A lot of people
really hated the character,

3
00:00:03,915 --> 00:00:06,055
(Wil:)and some of them
hated me because of it.

4
00:00:06,218 --> 00:00:07,028
(Wil:)I would do interviews,

5
00:00:07,185 --> 00:00:08,685
(Wil:)and people would be mean to me.

6
00:00:08,987 --> 00:00:10,937
(Sheldon:)That just happened to me.

7
00:00:11,089 --> 00:00:12,729
(Sheldon:)Next time you're stuck for a tweet,

8
00:00:12,891 --> 00:00:15,561
(Sheldon:)feel free to say
what a jerk Ira Flatow is.

9
00:00:16,194 --> 00:00:19,104
(Amy:)Sheldon, the point is
Wil learned to embrace

10
00:00:19,264 --> 00:00:22,404
(Amy:)that part of his life and
moved on to bigger and better things.

11
00:00:22,567 --> 00:00:23,907
(Wil:)Yeah, I'm an author now,

12
00:00:24,069 --> 00:00:25,449
(Wil:)I do public speaking,

13
00:00:25,604 --> 00:00:27,774
(Wil:)and I have my own web series
about board games.

14
00:00:29,174 --> 00:00:31,054
(Amy:)We're trying to cheer him up, so...

15
00:00:36,581 --> 00:00:37,851
(Wil:)I'm just saying
that there was a time

16
00:00:38,016 --> 00:00:40,356
(Wil:)when I thought I would never get
out of Wesley Crusher's shadow.

17
00:00:41,019 --> 00:00:44,129
(Wil:)But now, it's just one small part
of a pretty great life,

18
00:00:44,289 --> 00:00:46,269
(Wil:)and it's a part
that I'm happy is there.

19
00:00:46,791 --> 00:00:48,601
(Sheldon:)I do see what you're saying.

20
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:50,100
(Sheldon:)That helps.

21
00:00:50,262 --> 00:00:51,242
(Sheldon:)Good.

22
00:00:51,396 --> 00:00:53,466
(Sheldon:)Would you two like to stay
and play trains with ms?

23
00:00:53,632 --> 00:00:54,572
(Ira:)-Sure.
-Okay.

24
00:00:54,733 --> 00:00:55,643
Oh, great!

25
00:00:56,868 --> 00:01:00,018
(Sheldon:)Now... I work the controls.

